Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/apple-announces-ipad-mini-with-oled-display/">new iPad mini</a> features an Adaptive True Tone flash, bringing an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a> feature to Apple's smallest tablet for the first time.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/ipad-mini-dynamic-flash.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1073189" /><br/>
Unlike the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air</a>, the previous-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a> already featured a True Tone flash. Apple says the new Adaptive True Tone flash on the &zwnj;iPad mini&zwnj; improves photography and document scanning. It sits alongside a 12-megapixel Wide rear camera with Smart HDR 4 and support for recording 4K video at up to 60 frames per second.<br/>
<br/>
The Adaptive True Tone flash debuted on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2022/09/07/APPLE-UNVEILS-IPHONE-14-PRO/">iPhone 14 Pro and iPhone 14 Pro Max</a> in 2022. It features an array of nine LEDs that adjust its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2022/09/08/iphone-14-pro-tidbits-box-flash-more/">lighting pattern and intensity</a> according to the selected focal length, allowing illumination to better match the camera's field of view.<br/>
<br/>
The technology subsequently came to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/05/07/apple-announces-new-ipad-pro/">M4 iPad Pro in 2024</a>, where Apple highlighted its ability to improve document scans. When the camera detects a document obscured by a shadow, the &zwnj;iPad Pro&zwnj; captures multiple images using the Adaptive Flash and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/05/14/new-ipad-pro-and-ipad-air-day-one-update/">combines them into a clearer scan</a>.<br/>
<br/>
